entification, family, travel, food, renting an apartment, study, the weather, etc.). These topics are listed in the textbook's table of contents.  The student who successfully completes the two-course sequence will have mastered about 1000 basic words and will be able to: 1) understand and actively participate in conversations on a limited range of practical topics such as self-identification, family, school, work, the weather, travel, etc., 2) read and understand, with the help of a short list of words, passages of up to 180 words written in Arabic script, and 3) discuss orally in class and write a 50-word paragraph in Arabic.  The two-course sequence aims to take the student from the Novice to the Intermediate Mid level according to the ACTFL proficiency guidelines.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "ARAB 1200, ARAB 1201", "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2025FA, 2024FA, 2023FA, 2022FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2909, "crseId": 353414, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ARAB", "catalogNbr": "1203", "titleShort": "Intermediate Arabic I", "titleLong": "Intermediate Arabic I", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "AFLANG", "descr": "Africana Studies Lang", "descrformal": "Africana Studies Language", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies", "attrDescrShort": "ExplStudy"}, {"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "EULANG", "descr": "European Studies Lang",